## SQ-UPG-05 | dimension move: players logged out in yellowstone and hub come back there; dimension folders move
@group A
@boot 2
@commands Fixture also has: a player logged out in `creativeengineering:yellowstone` with a bed spawn there; a second player in `hub`; a waystone, a sky island and a meta structure (e.g. a balloon fleet) generated and forceloaded in the Overworld; `dimensions/creativeengineering/{yellowstone,hub,...}` on disk. Boot a copy on the new jars; both players log in; `/execute in creativeworldgen:yellowstone run say ok`; `/locate structure creativeworldgen:sky_island`; walk into the old sky island and meta structure; `/kill` the first player; `/save-all flush`; stop; `ls world/dimensions`
@pass Log: `[dimension-move] dimensions/creativeengineering/<dim> -> dimensions/creativeworldgen/<dim>` per dimension, `[legacy-ids]` key and chunk structure lines, `[swaps]` lines for `tune_spawns` / `bee_nests`; no `Unknown structure start`, `Found reference to unknown structure`, `Unknown structure piece id` or WorldGenSettings error. Players log in at their old spot (`Dimension` = `creativeworldgen:yellowstone`); respawn at the bed; terrain intact; old structures still count (spawns, `/locate` finds the old one); the waystone teleports into the moved dimension; after stop `world/dimensions/creativeengineering` is gone and level.dat names only `creativeworldgen:` dimensions. Record whether Xaero minimap data for those dimensions starts empty
@fails Dimension empty or regenerated: `LevelStorageAccessDimensionMoveMixin` not applied, or both folders existed (warning). Player in the Overworld: `ResourceKeyLegacyDimensionMixin`. Structure starts dropped: `ChunkSerializerLegacyStructuresMixin` / `StructureCheckLegacyStructuresMixin` SRG names
@from rows/NSM.qb SQ-NSM-07 (r1118 R3: was its fixture copy)
bootreject Unknown structure start|Found reference to unknown structure|Unknown structure piece id|WorldGenSettings.*(error|Error)
> pbot spawn nsmY 0 100 0 creativeworldgen:yellowstone survival
sleep 5
> pbot spawn nsmH 0 100 0 creativeworldgen:hub survival
sleep 5
> execute in creativeworldgen:yellowstone run say NSM07-yellowstone-ok
shell echo "dimension-move lines: $(grep -c '\[dimension-move\] dimensions/creativeengineering/' logs/latest.log)"; grep -E "\[legacy-ids\]" logs/latest.log | head -5 | cut -c1-240; L=$(sed -n "s/^level-name=//p" server.properties); ls "$L"/dimensions
expect NSM07-yellowstone-ok$
expect \[nsmprobe\] login nsmY dim creativeworldgen:yellowstone
expect \[nsmprobe\] login nsmH dim creativeworldgen:hub
reject \[nsmprobe\] login nsm[YH] dim minecraft:overworld
look 11 dimension-move lines; ls shows only creativeworldgen; nsmY's respawn (login line) is the bed in yellowstone; structure starts: RECORD not covered (fixture has none)

## SQ-UPG-06 | Creative Labels rename: notes, labels and the edited labels config carried
@group A
@boot 2
@commands Fixture built on `creativeLabels-1.0.1.jar` before the rename: a stone wall with 3 written, dyed notes (one special, one with its text erased), a label showing a diamond on a chest face, notes and an eraser in a chest and the player inventory; hand-edited `creative_labels-common.toml` (`noteLength` 20) and `creative_labels-client.toml` (`textDistance` 10). Boot a copy on the new jars; `/save-all flush`; reload the chunks; `/data get block <chest>`; check config/
@pass Log: `[creativelabels] config creative_labels-common.toml carried over`, `[swaps]` remap lines for `creative_labels:*`, no `[swaps] unresolved`, no block entity load error for `face_paper`. Every note keeps text, color, special and layer order; the label keeps its picture. Chest reads `creativelabels:sticky_note` with `CreativeLabels.Text` and `creativelabels:eraser`. `config/creativelabels-*.toml` hold 20 and 10, old files gone. `/give @s creativelabels:sticky_note` works
@fails Notes gone but block present: the `replaces` entry for `face_paper` (block entity alias). Config at defaults: `CreativeLabels.carryOverConfig` ran after the new file existed
@from rows/NSM.qb SQ-NSM-09 (r1118 R3: was its fixture copy)
bootexpect \[creativelabels\] config creative_labels-common.toml carried over
bootreject face_paper.*(Exception|[Ee]rror)|\[swaps\] .*unresolved
> forceload add 0 16 8 17
> save-all flush
waitlog Saved the game 120
> cdevtest be 1 -59 17
> cdevtest be 2 -59 17
> cdevtest be 3 -59 17
> cdevtest be 6 -60 17
> cdevtest inv 6 -60 16
shell grep -hE "^\s*(noteLength|textDistance)" config/creativelabels-*.toml; ls config | grep -c "creative_labels-" || true
count verb=be be=creativelabels:face_paper == 4
expect verb=be be=creativelabels:face_paper nbt=.*Kind:\\"label\\".*minecraft:diamond
expect verb=inv slot=\d+ item="?creativelabels:sticky_note\*1\{.*chest note
expect verb=inv slot=\d+ item="?creativelabels:eraser
reject \[cdevtest\] verb=\S+ done=0
look notes keep text, colour, special and layer order (Notes lists in the three wall lines); configs hold noteLength 20 and textDistance 10, old creative_labels files gone (count 0)

