expect verb=state pos=202,-60,200 state="rusticdelight:honey_pancakes\[facing=east,servings=7\]"
expect verb=state pos=204,-60,200 state="rusticdelight:cotton\[age=3\]"
expect verb=state pos=206,-60,200 state="rusticdelight:coffee\[age=4\]"
expect verb=state pos=208,-60,200 state="rusticdelight:bell_peppers\[age=6\]"
expect verb=state pos=210,-60,200 state=rusticdelight:bell_pepper_red_crate
expect verb=state pos=212,-60,200 state=rusticdelight:cotton_boll_crate
expect verb=state pos=214,-60,200 state=rusticdelight:potted_wild_coffee
expect verb=state pos=216,-60,200 state="rusticdelight:cherry_blossom_cheesecake\[bites=1,facing=north\]"
expect verb=state pos=218,-60,200 state=rusticdelight:wild_coffee
expect verb=state pos=220,-60,200 state=rusticdelight:glowing_calamari_crate
reject \[cdevtest\] verb=\S+ done=0
shell echo "missing-registry lines naming rusticdelight: $(grep -ciE '(missing|unidentified|unknown).*rusticdelight' logs/latest.log)"; grep -iE "(missing|unidentified|unknown).*rusticdelight" logs/latest.log | cut -c1-240 | head -8

## SQ-UPG-13 | Visceral Heap in new Nether chunks of a world made without Biomes O' Plenty
@group A
@boot 2
@commands the 1.2.02 server set had no Biomes O' Plenty (deploy/latest/verify/server.installed.sha1); boot 2 adds it: `locate biome biomesoplenty:visceral_heap` from 3000 64 3000 in the Nether, forceload, count flesh; RECORD
@pass RECORD whether the Heap appears in new chunks (plan section 9 question 1)
@fails `RegistryLoaderPresetOverworldMixin` comment against the `biome_config.json` readme
@from rows/VH.qb SQ-VH-11 (r1118 R3: was its fixture copy)
shell ls DIM-1/region 2>/dev/null | head -3; L=$(sed -n "s/^level-name=//p" server.properties); ls "$L"/DIM-1/region 2>/dev/null | wc -l
> execute in minecraft:the_nether positioned 3000 64 3000 run locate biome biomesoplenty:visceral_heap
waitlog (The nearest biomesoplenty:visceral_heap is at|Could not find a biome of type) 120
capture P is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run forceload add {P1} {P3}
sleep 15
> cdevtest state {P1} 64 {P3} dim=minecraft:the_nether
> cdevtest count {P1-8} 5 {P3-8} {P1+8} 120 {P3+8} biomesoplenty:flesh dim=minecraft:the_nether
> cdevtest count {P1-8} 5 {P3-8} {P1+8} 120 {P3+8} minecraft:netherrack dim=minecraft:the_nether
expect verb=count block=biomesoplenty:flesh n=[1-9]
expect verb=state pos=\S+ .*biome=biomesoplenty:visceral_heap
reject \[cdevtest\] verb=\S+ done=0
look RECORD: locate answer and distance from 3000 3000; flesh present in the newly generated chunk

@@section 2
@@title SQ-UPG 1.2.02 upgrade, Creative Delight namespace move: the CDNS fixture on the 1.2.02 release, scanned before and after, 2026-11-18 ([plan_cd_namespace.md](../plan_cd_namespace.md) 5, [plan_rowfix_r1118.md](../plan_rowfix_r1118.md) section 4; TODO `generators-and-tests #23`)
@@date 2026-11-18
@@reviewed 2026-11-20
@@jars creativecommon creativedelight
@@sources feature_writeup/plan_cd_namespace.md feature_writeup/plan_rowfix_r1118.md
@@tier T3
@@modset release_1202
@@prep run bash "$INST/tools/scratch_query/cdns_fixture.sh" "$OUT" "$INST/development/creativeDelight/src/main/resources/data/creativedelight/swaps/cd_namespace.json"
@@prep boot=2: modset pack
@@text
@@text Its own world: the CDNS fixture (cdns_fixture.js) fills x 0..127 like the NSM one. Boot 1 builds it on the 1.2.02 pack
@@text and scans the save (`cdns_probe.py scan`, baseline); boot 2 (current jars) and boot 3 (again) scan and compare. Replaces
@@text the cdns_step2 / cdns_full jar fixtures and their run scripts (cdns_step2_run.sh, cdns_full_run.sh).
@@text
@@table
## SQ-UPG-14 | boot 1 (1.2.02 jars): build the CDNS fixture (FULL BUILD: blocks, vanilla holders, every moved id, entities, bots, Cooking for Blockheads and remainder buffer) and scan it
@group A
@commands `/cdnsfix blocks vanilla allids entities bots pack pack2 manifest`; `save-all flush`; `cdns_probe.py scan` of the save into `OUT/upg_cdns_b1.json`
@pass every `[cdnsfix]` step OK (MISSING lines name ids the 1.2.02 jars lack, recorded); the scan writes the baseline
@fails a step failing: `tools/scratch_query/cdns_fixture.js` against the 1.2.02 jars
@absent creativeengineering:wooden_bucket creativeengineering:wooden_water_bucket (1.2.02 ids the fixture places on purpose)
> gamerule doMobSpawning false
> forceload add 0 0 127 127
sleep 10
> cdnsfix blocks
> cdnsfix vanilla
> cdnsfix allids
> cdnsfix entities
> cdnsfix bots
sleep 3
> cdnsfix pack
> cdnsfix pack2
> cdnsfix manifest
waitlog \[cdnsfix\] OK.*manifest 60
sleep 30
> save-all flush
waitlog Saved the game 120
shell L=$(sed -n "s/^level-name=//p" server.properties); python3 -I "$INST/tools/scratch_query/cdns_probe.py" scan "$L" ../upg_cdns_b1.json | tail -2
reject \[cdnsfix\] CMDFAIL|Unknown or incomplete command
look the [cdnsfix] MISSING lines (ids the 1.2.02 jars do not have) and the scan summary
## SQ-UPG-15 | boot 2 (current jars): every moved CD id read back, holders and blocks equal to boot 1, caps under creativedelight (SQ-CDNS-01, -03, -09)
@group A
@boot 2
@commands boot on the current jars; bot `cdnsOn` logs in again; hold 60 s; `save-all flush`; scan; `cdns_probe.py compare` boot 1 against boot 2
@pass Log: `[swaps]` remap lines for the moved ids, `[swaps] N permanent alias(es)` with N > 0, `[swaps] load report: every listed id resolved`, no `[swaps] unresolved`; compare exits 0 (holders and the block census equal); no `creativeengineering:corner_storage` / `remainder_buffer` capability key in the boot 2 scan
@fails `swap/SwapRemapper.java`, `swap/SwapReport.java`, `SwapCapabilityKeysMixin`, `SwapLists.renameCapabilityKeys`; compare names the holder and id
@from rows/CDNS.qb SQ-CDNS-01, -03, -09 (r1118 R3: were step2 / full jar fixture runs)
bootexpect \[swaps\] .*remapped
bootreject \[swaps\] .*unresolved
> forceload add 0 0 127 127
> pbot spawn cdnsOn 2 -60 20 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 60
> data get block 0 -60 16
> data get block 2 -60 16
> save-all flush
waitlog Saved the game 120
shell grep -hE "\[swaps\]" logs/latest.log | cut -c1-240 | head -12
shell L=$(sed -n "s/^level-name=//p" server.properties); python3 -I "$INST/tools/scratch_query/cdns_probe.py" scan "$L" ../upg_cdns_b2.json | tail -2; python3 -I "$INST/tools/scratch_query/cdns_probe.py" compare ../upg_cdns_b1.json ../upg_cdns_b2.json | tail -20
shell ! grep -qE '"creativeengineering:(corner_storage|remainder_buffer)"' ../upg_cdns_b2.json
look compare lines (exit 0 = EQUAL); ids still under creativeengineering in the scan only for stacks nothing decoded this boot (nested NBT, drive cells, data/*.dat)
## SQ-UPG-16 | boot 3 (current jars again): no second remap, the save stays equal (SQ-CDNS-04)
@group A
@boot 3
@commands boot again on the same jars; `save-all flush`; scan; compare with boot 2
@pass no `[swaps] ... remapped` line for the moved ids (already saved under the new ids); compare boot 2 against boot 3 exits 0; no `[swaps] unresolved`
@fails a remap line again: the saved snapshot still names the old id, or the alias hides it
@from rows/CDNS.qb SQ-CDNS-04 (r1118 R3)
bootreject \[swaps\] .*unresolved
bootreject \[swaps\] minecraft:item: \d+ id\(s\) remapped
> forceload add 0 0 127 127
> pbot spawn cdnsOn 2 -60 20 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 30
> save-all flush
waitlog Saved the game 120
shell L=$(sed -n "s/^level-name=//p" server.properties); python3 -I "$INST/tools/scratch_query/cdns_probe.py" scan "$L" ../upg_cdns_b3.json | tail -2; python3 -I "$INST/tools/scratch_query/cdns_probe.py" compare ../upg_cdns_b2.json ../upg_cdns_b3.json | tail -20
